// The Falcon low-level layer: FFT, the modular NTT, the bignum helpers, the
// constant tables, the Merkle tree and the verify internals.
//
// This package is `internal` in the compiler-enforced sense: MoonBit applies the
// Go-style rule, so only packages under cc06b/mooncry/ can import it. A
// downstream consumer writing `import "cc06b/mooncry/internal"` gets
//   Cannot import internal package cc06b/mooncry/internal ... due to internal
//   visibility rules
// which is the point: these 80-odd names are implementation, verified layer by
// layer against the C reference, and they are free to change.
//
// It has no imports of its own -- the layer is self-contained apart from the
// core prelude. The one Falcon file that needs the library SHAKE XOF
// (falcon_common.mbt) stays in lib, which keeps the dependency one-way:
// lib -> internal, never the reverse (MoonBit rejects import cycles).
